// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/automation/crm-duet.t27 -- a REAL Telegram dialogue between two agents: the owner's
// seller agent (from the platform owner's account) sells every function of the bot to a
// connected seller acting as a new buyer (answered by a persona model from HER session), and
// the content offered is for HER real game -- Leela Chakra
// (@leela_chakra_ai_bot, mini app t27.ai/leela, 72 planes, entry with a six, ruleset classic).
// Host: 999-multibots-telegraf apps/vibee-editor/render/src/agent/crm-duet-tool.ts -- owner-only
//       tools crm_duet (starts a run in the background, returns its id) and crm_duet_status
//       (transcript, tool coverage, media sent, paid calls). Seller turns are runAgent with the
//       owner's ToolContext and surface "business" (no button markers, sales playbook applies);
//       buyer turns are one plain completion on resolveProvider() with the buyer persona.
//       Sessions come from tg_sessions by id (crm-sellers.t27); sends go through the same
//       address-book warm-up as owner-button proposals (tg-proposals.ts).
// WHY the seller speaks first: the production business bot answers any DM to the owner, but
// pauses for OWNER_TAKEOVER_MS (30 min) after a message typed by the owner himself. A duet that
// opens from the owner's session puts the business bot on hold, so the buyer's replies are
// answered by the duet's seller agent and not twice. A duet that let the buyer open would race it.
// WHY it is an exception to the proposal rule: owner buttons are the normal path for a send.
// Here the owner authorises the whole run in advance (confirm before each run), the tool is
// owner-only, both accounts are connected sellers (the row in tg_sessions is the consent), and
// the transcript is returned; session strings never are.
// Coverage: every tool the seller agent calls is recorded name -> ok/fail; paid generations
// (since v5: every call of a tool with a price > 0, and of crm_story_reel only a call that
// starts a reel) are counted; the
// brief asks for at most one per reply and two per run (one portrait from her face, one reel
// -- the brief since 2026-09-21; v1 said three) -- a SOFT cap enforced by the prompt and
// measured in the report, not a hard limit in code.
// Claim status: tool written and unit-tested with doubles. Whether a run SUCCEEDED live -- both
// sessions alive, the business bot silent, content delivered -- is shown by crm_duet_status,
// not by this file.
// v2 (2026-09-27): bound to the host (src/spec/crm-duet.test.ts runs every test below against
// crm-duet-tool.ts, leela-canon.ts and the bot's businessBotService.ts). v1's tests were
// braceless -- inert under the parser of the day -- and its SELLER/BUYER constants were two
// real people's Telegram ids; they are roles now, and the host imports the turn limits,
// the retry and the discovery gate from here instead of restating them. Binding found two
// drifts, both settled on the side of this file: the host's negation window reached THREE
// words back ("bez vsyakikh tochnykh predskazanij" passed), now it takes NEGATION_WINDOW_WORDS
// from here; and the brief's soft cap had been two per run since the portrait came first.
// v3 (2026-09-27): THE DUET'S REEL IS THE STORY REEL. Owner, 2026-09-27: "why does the agent
// not understand the video made of three frames -- it keeps doing it the old way". The seller
// brief said "only the LeelaPlanReel template"; it now names crm_story_reel (three frames, her
// face in a new setting each, her voice, a pause with the call), the topic a plan she chose.
// The silent plan reel is not offered. Wiring the new route found four holes the old one hid:
//   1. crm_story_reel was in no set of the duet: listed on discovery turns, callable on a
//      rewrite round, not counted. It joins the paid set; only a call that STARTS a reel is a
//      paid call -- the readiness read is free, but it waits for discovery with the rest.
//   2. its card reaches the owner's Telegram, and a dry run sends nothing: not in a dry run.
//   3. it is made in the background (5-10 min) and comes to the OWNER as a card "to her DM" --
//      one press, his; the duet forwards nothing. Where the card goes is the duet's (the tool
//      context), not the model's: a model's `to` could bind a group of hers. A line promising
//      to send it is kept by that card, so the duet does not "keep" it by resending the last
//      file it has -- which was her portrait. The next seller turn is told it is being made.
//   4. her plan: v2 moved only cards of the LeelaPlanReel template. A reel for plan N now goes
//      to her REEL card for plan N whatever reel template it names; a card with no template is
//      her own and is never moved. A story reel without a topic takes her next card itself
//      (story template), and the duet links nothing then -- one card, not two.
// v4 (2026-10-06): A DRY RUN IS FREE. Owner, 2026-10-06 (translated): "a dry run must be free,
// change the spec". v3 kept only the story reel out of a dry run; every other paid tool was
// offered from seller turn 2 on, so a run that sends nothing still paid for generations
// (duet-mu027xqr, a full dry run, made one paid call). Now a dry run offers no paid tool on
// ANY seller turn, and a paid call that arrives anyway is refused by the dispatcher the way a
// discovery turn refuses it: an error the model can act on, no handler runs, nothing is
// charged. A real run is unchanged: discovery first, paid tools from seller turn 2. The host
// reads dry_run as true unless the caller passed the boolean false (999#3794), so the free
// path is also the default one.
// v5 (2026-10-06): A PAID TOOL IS ONE WITH A PRICE, NOT ONE ON A LIST. v4 hid the six tools
// v1 named and stopped there; the seller is offered the whole registry, and four tools that
// charge were on no list: lipsync_generate (charges by the second), story_reel and split_reel
// (they borrow tools that charge), crm_voice_clone (the one-time clone price). A dry run still
// offered them on every turn (reviewer, t27#6897). The rule is now stated on the price, so it
// cannot drift as tools are added: any tool whose price is > 0 -- its own entry in the
// render's price table, or the highest price of a tool it borrows -- is a paid tool, hidden and
// refused on every turn of a dry run and on discovery turns. The host derives the set from
// its price table and registry; this file no longer counts them (PAID_TOOLS = 6 is gone).
// story_offered is paid_tool_offered by definition: the story reel follows the paid gate.
// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module automation::crm_duet {

    pub const KIND : str = "automation";
    pub const ID : str = "crm-duet";
    pub const REPO : str = "999-multibots-telegraf";
    pub const VERSION : u8 = 5;

    // ---- Who ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const SELLER : str = "platform-owner";  // the owner's account: sells
    pub const BUYER : str = "connected-seller";  // a connected seller who plays a new buyer
    pub const BUYER_GAME : str = "Leela Chakra";
    pub const BUYER_BOT : str = "leela_chakra_ai_bot";
    pub const BUYER_APP : str = "https://t27.ai/leela/";
    pub const LEELA_PLANES : u8 = 72;
    pub const LEELA_RULESET : str = "classic";

    // ---- The tools ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const TOOL_START : str = "crm_duet";
    pub const TOOL_STATUS : str = "crm_duet_status";
    pub const TOOL_CALLER : str = "owner";  // requireOwner
    pub const BUYER_MUST_BE_SELLER : bool = true;  // row in tg_sessions
    pub const BUYER_MAY_BE_OWNER : bool = false;
    pub const RUNS_IN_BACKGROUND : bool = true;  // start returns at once; status reads the run
    pub const TURNS_DEFAULT : u8 = 4;  // seller+buyer pairs
    pub const TURNS_MAX : u8 = 8;
    pub const SELLER_SPEAKS_FIRST : bool = true;
    pub const SELLER_SURFACE : str = "business";
    pub const BUYER_TURN_IS_PLAIN_COMPLETION : bool = true;  // no tools on the buyer's side
    pub const DRY_RUN_SENDS : bool = false;  // dry_run: agents talk, Telegram receives nothing
    pub const REPORT_TO_OWNER_SAVED : bool = true;  // final report from the owner's session to "me"
    pub const RETURNS_SESSION : bool = false;

    // ---- Why the seller opens -------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const BUSINESS_BOT_TAKEOVER_MIN : u8 = 30;  // OWNER_TAKEOVER_MS in businessBotService.ts

    // ---- Coverage -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // v5: a tool is paid when its price is > 0 (the render's price table, directly or through a
    // tool it borrows). There is no hand list and no count here: a count is what drifted.
    pub const PAID_TOOL_IS_PRICED : bool = true;
    pub const PAID_TOOLS_HAND_LIST : bool = false;
    pub const PAID_PER_REPLY_SOFT : u8 = 1;
    pub const PAID_PER_RUN_SOFT : u8 = 2;  // one portrait, one reel
    pub const PAID_CAP_IS_HARD : bool = false;
    pub const MEDIA_FORWARDED : bool = true;  // a tool result with done=true and an http url is sent as a file

    // ---- The reel is the story reel (v3) ---------------------------------------------------
    pub const REEL_TOOL : str = "crm_story_reel";
    pub const OLD_REEL_IN_BRIEF : bool = false;  // the brief no longer says "only LeelaPlanReel"
    pub const STORY_PAID_ONLY_ON_START : bool = true;  // start=true spends; the readiness read is free
    pub const STORY_HIDDEN_IN_DISCOVERY : bool = true;  // the whole tool, the read included
    pub const STORY_IN_DRY_RUN : bool = false;  // its card would reach the owner's Telegram
    pub const STORY_START_COUNTS_AS_WORK : bool = true;  // "I am putting it together" after a start is not a false claim
    pub const STORY_REEL_FORWARDED : bool = false;  // made in 5-10 min, comes to the owner as a card
    pub const STORY_CARD_TO : str = "dm";  // set by the duet in the tool context, never by the model
    pub const STORY_START_KEEPS_PROMISE : bool = true;  // a promise to send it is kept by the owner's card; nothing is resent
    pub const STORY_NOTE_NEXT_TURN : bool = true;  // the seller hears it is being made, not ready
    pub const PLAN_LINK_ANY_REEL_TEMPLATE : bool = true;  // v2 read only LeelaPlanReel cards
    pub const PLAN_LINK_OWN_CARDS : bool = false;  // a card with no template is hers: never moved
    pub const STORY_WITHOUT_TOPIC_TAKES_CARD : bool = true;  // the story template takes her next card; the duet links none

    // ---- Honesty of the seller line (duet-mtzyg2t6, 2026-09-13) ---------------------------
    // Turn 0 of a dry run said "I already built a trial reel in your style and am preparing
    // it for publication" -- the only tools called were crm_client_profile and
    // crm_lead_context, no reel existed. promisesFile() catches "I am sending the file";
    // it does not catch "the work is done". A claim of finished work is honest only when
    // the same turn called a producing tool or forwarded media.
    pub const CLAIMED_WORK_NEEDS_TOOL : bool = true;
    pub const CLAIM_CHECK_CORRECTIONS : u8 = 1;  // one rewrite round, as the voice check; the second miss is sent and reported
    pub const CLAIM_MISS_IS_VIOLATION : bool = true;  // both misses land in violations, the corrected one marked as rewritten

    // New constants from the live run (duet-mub68idg, 2026-09-21)
    pub const FEED_PUBLISH_SAYS_SAVED : bool = true;  // a hidden save is reported as saved and waiting, never as published
    pub const NO_LIVED_EXPERIENCE_CLAIM : bool = true;  // the seller may speak about the product and the canon, never claim personal practice or a human's experience
    pub const PLAN_MEANING_FROM_CANON : bool = true;  // a plan's meaning in a seller line is taken from the leela_plan result of the same turn, never paraphrased from memory
    pub const PERSONA_CONSENT_IS_NOT_CONSENT : bool = true;  // the persona's agreement never counts as the client's approval
    pub const AGENT_PUBLISH_IS_HIDDEN : bool = true;  // an agent publish is always hidden until a human approves

    // ---- State of a run that broke off (same run) ----------------------------------------
    // Turn 2: every provider answered with a rate limit, the seller produced no text, the
    // loop broke and the run was stored as done with 3 of 8 lines and no error. The
    // dashboard showed "finished, 0 violations". A run that did not play every turn is
    // failed, and the turn's error is the run's error.
    pub const ABORTED_RUN_STATE : str = "failed";
    pub const ABORTED_RUN_KEEPS_ERROR : bool = true;
    pub const DONE_MEANS_ALL_LINES : bool = true;  // done only when the transcript has turns * 2 lines
    pub const RUN_ERROR_SHOWN_ON_DASHBOARD : bool = true;  // crm_duet_runs returns error; the client dashboard prints it

    // ---- One pause and one retry on a provider limit (duet-mu00klri, 2026-09-13) ----------
    // Third run of the day to die on the same wall: every provider answered with a limit
    // ("request limit exceeded" -- 429 -- from z.ai twice, "Worker local total request limit
    // reached (16/16)" from NVIDIA), the seller had already called five free tools and
    // produced no text. A limit is temporary; a seller turn that hits one waits once and
    // plays the turn again from the same history. Anything else (bad key, no balance,
    // unknown model) is not retried -- waiting would not change the answer.
    pub const SELLER_RETRY_ON_LIMIT : u8 = 1;  // one retry per seller turn, never more
    pub const SELLER_RETRY_PAUSE_MS : u32 = 30000;
    pub const RETRY_ONLY_WITHOUT_PAID_CALL : bool = true;  // a turn that already paid for a generation is not replayed
    pub const RETRY_NOTED_IN_TRANSCRIPT : bool = true;  // the transcript line keeps `retried: "<first error>"`
    pub const LIMIT_MARKERS : str = "429|limit|ResourceExhausted|too many requests";  // case-insensitive; "limit" covers "rate limit" and "limit reached"
    pub const LIMIT_MARKER_RU_DIAGNOSE : bool = true;  // provider.ts diagnose() renders 429 in Russian ("... limit zaprosov"); that word is matched too

    // ---- Discovery gate (duet-mu027xqr, 2026-09-14) -----------------------------------------
    // First run to play all 8 lines. The seller's line 0 opened with a paid reel_render
    // (70 s, one token) and "the same style you liked" -- nothing had been shown or liked;
    // the buyer caught it, the seller apologised on line 2. The brief said "first 1-2 lines
    // are discovery only"; the model did not hold it. The gate is in code: on the first
    // DISCOVERY_SELLER_TURNS seller turns the paid tools are not offered to the model and a
    // call that arrives anyway is refused by the dispatcher; a familiarity claim gets one
    // rewrite, as the claim check, and both misses are violations.
    pub const DISCOVERY_SELLER_TURNS : u8 = 2;  // seller turns 0 and 1 (transcript lines 0 and 2)
    pub const DISCOVERY_HIDES_PAID_TOOLS : bool = true;  // toOpenAITools does not list them on those turns
    pub const DISCOVERY_REFUSES_PAID_CALL : bool = true;  // a paid call on those turns answers with an error, no handler runs, nothing is spent
    // v4: a dry run is free. No paid tool on any seller turn of a dry run; a call that
    // arrives anyway is refused as in discovery.
    pub const DRY_RUN_SPENDS : bool = false;
    pub const DRY_RUN_HIDES_PAID_TOOLS : bool = true;  // toOpenAITools does not list them on any turn of a dry run
    pub const DRY_RUN_REFUSES_PAID_CALL : bool = true;  // error to the model, no handler runs, nothing is charged
    pub const FAMILIARITY_MARKERS_RU : str = "ponravil|dogovar|dogovoril|kak vy prosili|po vashej pros'be|obsuzhdali|kak my reshili";  // transliterated; the code holds the Cyrillic regex
    pub const FAMILIARITY_CORRECTIONS : u8 = 1;
    pub const FAMILIARITY_MISS_IS_VIOLATION : bool = true;

    // ---- The seller's voice (same run) ------------------------------------------------------
    // Line 2 "ya ne videl" (masculine), line 4 "ya zadavala ... sama ... ne videla" (feminine):
    // the writer writes for the owner, Dmitrii, and the brief now says so. A feminine
    // first-person past form in a seller line is reported as a voice flag, not rewritten.
    pub const SELLER_GENDER : str = "m";
    pub const SELLER_GENDER_IN_BRIEF : bool = true;
    pub const GENDER_SLIP_IS_FLAG_ONLY : bool = true;

    // ---- Negation in the stop-list, and the hook (same run) ---------------------------------
    // Line 6 "bez obeshchanij i bez predskazanij" was flagged for "predskaz": a claim word
    // under negation is not a claim. The voice check skips a CLAIM word preceded within two
    // words by a negation (bez / ne / net / nikakikh / ni / nikogda). Pressure words and
    // prices are not exempted -- "not today" still presses. The plan-6 hook "Ne sluchajno."
    // reads as prophecy (client lesson of 2026-09-13); the brief forbids it by name and asks
    // for a hook that names the square, not a verdict about the reader.
    pub const CLAIM_NEGATION_EXEMPT : bool = true;
    pub const NEGATION_WINDOW_WORDS : u8 = 2;
    pub const PRESSURE_NEGATION_EXEMPT : bool = false;
    pub const HOOK_NE_SLUCHAJNO_FORBIDDEN_IN_BRIEF : bool = true;

    // ---- Seen live ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const DRY_RUN_SEEN_LIVE : bool = true;  // duet-mtzyg2t6 started from /crm/435572800, 3 lines, nothing sent
    pub const RUN_KILLED_BY_REDEPLOY_SEEN : bool = true;  // duet-mtzy6kao: vibee-render redeployed 21 s after start, 0 lines, stays running until lost
    pub const FAILED_STATE_SEEN_LIVE : bool = true;  // duet-mu00klri: state failed, error "turn 0: ...", dashboard shows the failed badge and lines 1/8
    pub const CLAIM_CHECK_SEEN_LIVE : bool = false;  // the seller never spoke in that run; unit tests only
    pub const RETRY_SEEN_LIVE : bool = false;  // a transcript line with `retried` from a real run is the evidence
    pub const FULL_DRY_RUN_SEEN_LIVE : bool = true;  // duet-mu027xqr: state done, 8/8 lines, 1 paid call, 0 violations, 1 voice flag
    // duet-mu2qj57q (2026-09-15, vibee-render e2c4617, dry run, 4 turns, state done, 8/8 lines): seller
    // lines 0 and 2 called only crm_client_profile, crm_lead_context, my_renders, providers_status and
    // asked one question each; the single paid call (reel_render) came on line 4 after the buyer asked
    // for an example; line 0 was rewritten once ("ssylka na nesushchestvuyushchuyu dogovorennost'").
    pub const DISCOVERY_GATE_SEEN_LIVE : bool = true;
    pub const DISCOVERY_GATE_LIVE_RUN : str = "duet-mu2qj57q";
    pub const FAMILIARITY_REWRITE_SEEN_LIVE : bool = true;  // same run, violations[0] is the turn 0 rewrite
    pub const SELLER_GENDER_FIXED_SEEN_LIVE : bool = true;  // same run, line 0 "Ya Dmitrij", line 6 "Rad" -- no feminine slip in 4 seller lines
    // Open debt seen in the same run: line 4 says "the video is already in the chat as the next message"
    // while dry_run sends nothing (media_sent 0). promisesFile() does not catch "already in the chat".
    pub const DRY_RUN_DELIVERY_CLAIM_SEEN : bool = true;
    pub const DRY_RUN_DELIVERY_CLAIM_FIXED : bool = false;

    // ---- Not claimed ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const DUET_RAN_LIVE : bool = true;  // crm_duet_status of a real (non-dry) run is the evidence
    pub const DUET_LIVE_RUN : str = "duet-mub68idg";  // the first live run

    struct Turn {
        from_owner: bool,
        index: u8,
    }

    // The duet alternates and the seller holds every even index, starting at 0.
    fn speaker_at(i: u8) -> Turn {
        return Turn { from_owner: i % 2 == 0, index: i };
    }

    // Whether a paid tool is offered to the seller model on seller turn `seller_turn`.
    // A dry run is free (v4): never, on any turn.
    fn paid_tool_offered(seller_turn: u8, dry_run: bool) -> bool {
        return !dry_run && seller_turn >= DISCOVERY_SELLER_TURNS;
    }

    // Whether the dispatcher refuses a paid call that arrives anyway: on a turn that does
    // not offer paid tools, and on every rewrite round (a rewrite changes words, not work).
    fn paid_call_refused(seller_turn: u8, dry_run: bool, rewrite: bool) -> bool {
        return rewrite || !paid_tool_offered(seller_turn, dry_run);
    }

    // Whether a tool is a paid tool: its price is > 0. The price is the host's, never a list.
    fn tool_is_paid(price: u32) -> bool {
        return price > 0;
    }

    // The price of a tool that borrows another: the higher of its own and the borrowed one's.
    // A tool that charges nothing itself but runs one that charges is a paid tool.
    fn borrowed_price(own: u32, borrowed: u32) -> u32 {
        if own >= borrowed {
            return own;
        }
        return borrowed;
    }

    // Whether a tool with this price is offered on seller turn `seller_turn`: a free tool
    // always, a priced one only where paid tools are offered (never in a dry run).
    fn priced_tool_offered(price: u32, seller_turn: u8, dry_run: bool) -> bool {
        return !tool_is_paid(price) || paid_tool_offered(seller_turn, dry_run);
    }

    // Whether a call is a paid generation: the story reel only when it starts one.
    fn call_is_paid(paid_tool: bool, story_reel: bool, start: bool) -> bool {
        if story_reel {
            return start;
        }
        return paid_tool;
    }

    // Whether the story reel is offered to the seller on seller turn `seller_turn`.
    // It follows the paid gate (v5): one rule, not a second copy of it.
    fn story_offered(seller_turn: u8, dry_run: bool) -> bool {
        return paid_tool_offered(seller_turn, dry_run);
    }

    // Whether the duet keeps a promise to send a file by resending the last one it has.
    fn resend_for_promise(media_in_turn: u8, story_started: bool, has_last_file: bool) -> bool {
        return media_in_turn == 0 && !story_started && has_last_file;
    }

    // Whether one of her open cards takes a reel for a plan: a reel card about that plan.
    fn card_takes_reel(names_plan: bool, has_template: bool) -> bool {
        return names_plan && has_template;
    }

    // The plan a story reel is about (0 = none): the plan its topic names, else the one plan
    // looked up this run. No topic: the story template takes her next card itself.
    fn story_plan(topic_given: bool, plan_in_topic: u8, looked_up_single: u8) -> u8 {
        if !topic_given {
            return 0;
        }
        if plan_in_topic > 0 {
            return plan_in_topic;
        }
        return looked_up_single;
    }

    // Whether a CLAIM-word hit counts, given how many words back the nearest negation stands
    // (0 = none in the window).
    fn claim_hit_counts(negation_distance: u8) -> bool {
        return negation_distance == 0 || negation_distance > NEGATION_WINDOW_WORDS;
    }

    // Whether a claim of finished work in a turn that produced nothing is a miss.
    fn claim_is_honest(claims_done_work: bool, producing_tool_called: bool, media_forwarded: bool) -> bool {
        return !claims_done_work || producing_tool_called || media_forwarded;
    }

    // Whether a failed seller turn is played again: once, only on a limit, only when no
    // paid generation happened in the failed attempt.
    fn retry_allowed(retries_done: u8, is_limit: bool, paid_calls_in_attempt: u8) -> bool {
        return retries_done < SELLER_RETRY_ON_LIMIT && is_limit && paid_calls_in_attempt == 0;
    }

    // The state a finished loop stores: done only for a full transcript, failed otherwise.
    fn state_after(lines: u8, turns: u8, errored: bool) -> str {
        if errored || lines < turns * 2 {
            return ABORTED_RUN_STATE;
        }
        return "done";
    }

    // Whether the business bot stays silent during a duet run
    fn business_bot_silent(is_owner_session: bool, takeover_minutes: u8) -> bool {
        return is_owner_session && takeover_minutes <= BUSINESS_BOT_TAKEOVER_MIN;
    }

    test "the seller opens and the business bot stays silent for the run" {
        assert(SELLER_SPEAKS_FIRST);
        assert(speaker_at(0).from_owner);
        assert(!speaker_at(1).from_owner);
        assert(speaker_at(2).from_owner);
        assert(business_bot_silent(true, 12));
        assert(!business_bot_silent(false, 12));
        assert(!business_bot_silent(true, 31));
    }

    test "the run is the owner's, needs a connected buyer who is not the owner, and returns no session" {
        assert(TOOL_CALLER == "owner");
        assert(BUYER_MUST_BE_SELLER);
        assert(!BUYER_MAY_BE_OWNER);
        assert(!RETURNS_SESSION);
        assert(SELLER == "platform-owner");
        assert(BUYER == "connected-seller");
    }

    test "the paid cap is soft and says so" {
        assert(!PAID_CAP_IS_HARD);
        assert(PAID_PER_REPLY_SOFT == 1);
        assert(PAID_PER_RUN_SOFT == 2);
        assert(PAID_TOOL_IS_PRICED);
        assert(!PAID_TOOLS_HAND_LIST);
    }

    test "the duet's reel is the story reel, paid only when it starts" {
        assert(REEL_TOOL == "crm_story_reel");
        assert(!OLD_REEL_IN_BRIEF);
        assert(STORY_PAID_ONLY_ON_START);
        assert(call_is_paid(true, true, true));
        assert(!call_is_paid(true, true, false));  // the readiness read is free
        assert(call_is_paid(true, false, false));  // reel_render: every call
        assert(!call_is_paid(false, false, false));  // leela_plan
        assert(STORY_START_COUNTS_AS_WORK);
    }

    test "the story reel waits for discovery and never runs dry" {
        assert(STORY_HIDDEN_IN_DISCOVERY);
        assert(!STORY_IN_DRY_RUN);
        assert(!story_offered(0, false));
        assert(!story_offered(1, false));
        assert(story_offered(2, false));
        assert(!story_offered(2, true));
    }

    test "the story reel reaches her by the owner's card, and a promise is not a resend" {
        assert(!STORY_REEL_FORWARDED);
        assert(STORY_CARD_TO == "dm");
        assert(STORY_START_KEEPS_PROMISE);
        assert(STORY_NOTE_NEXT_TURN);
        assert(resend_for_promise(0, false, true));
        assert(!resend_for_promise(0, true, true));
        assert(!resend_for_promise(1, false, true));
        assert(!resend_for_promise(0, false, false));
    }

    test "her reel card is found by the plan, not by the template" {
        assert(PLAN_LINK_ANY_REEL_TEMPLATE);
        assert(!PLAN_LINK_OWN_CARDS);
        assert(card_takes_reel(true, true));
        assert(!card_takes_reel(true, false));  // her own card
        assert(!card_takes_reel(false, true));
        assert(STORY_WITHOUT_TOPIC_TAKES_CARD);
        assert(story_plan(true, 6, 0) == 6);
        assert(story_plan(true, 0, 12) == 12);
        assert(story_plan(true, 6, 12) == 6);  // her words over the lookup
        assert(story_plan(false, 0, 12) == 0);  // no topic: the template's own card
        assert(story_plan(true, 0, 0) == 0);
    }

    test "turns are bounded and the buyer side never calls tools" {
        assert(TURNS_DEFAULT <= TURNS_MAX);
        assert(TURNS_MAX == 8);
        assert(BUYER_TURN_IS_PLAIN_COMPLETION);
        assert(RUNS_IN_BACKGROUND);
    }

    test "a run that broke off is failed and keeps the turn's error" {
        assert(ABORTED_RUN_STATE == "failed");
        assert(ABORTED_RUN_KEEPS_ERROR);
        assert(DONE_MEANS_ALL_LINES);
        assert(state_after(3, 4, true) == "failed");
        assert(state_after(3, 4, false) == "failed");
        assert(state_after(6, 4, false) == "failed");  // 6 of 8 lines: turns * 2, not turns
        assert(state_after(8, 4, false) == "done");
        assert(RUN_ERROR_SHOWN_ON_DASHBOARD);
    }

    test "a claim of finished work needs a tool or a file in the same turn" {
        assert(CLAIMED_WORK_NEEDS_TOOL);
        assert(CLAIM_CHECK_CORRECTIONS == 1);
        assert(CLAIM_MISS_IS_VIOLATION);
        assert(!claim_is_honest(true, false, false));
        assert(claim_is_honest(true, true, false));
        assert(claim_is_honest(true, false, true));
        assert(claim_is_honest(false, false, false));
    }

    test "a seller turn that hit a limit is retried once, without paid calls" {
        assert(SELLER_RETRY_ON_LIMIT == 1);
        assert(SELLER_RETRY_PAUSE_MS == 30000);
        assert(RETRY_ONLY_WITHOUT_PAID_CALL);
        assert(RETRY_NOTED_IN_TRANSCRIPT);
        assert(retry_allowed(0, true, 0));
        assert(!retry_allowed(1, true, 0));
        assert(!retry_allowed(0, false, 0));
        assert(!retry_allowed(0, true, 1));
    }

    test "the first two seller turns are discovery: no paid tools, no familiarity" {
        assert(DISCOVERY_SELLER_TURNS == 2);
        assert(DISCOVERY_HIDES_PAID_TOOLS);
        assert(DISCOVERY_REFUSES_PAID_CALL);
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(0, false));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(1, false));
        assert(paid_tool_offered(2, false));
        assert(FAMILIARITY_CORRECTIONS == 1);
        assert(FAMILIARITY_MISS_IS_VIOLATION);
        assert(SELLER_GENDER == "m");
        assert(SELLER_GENDER_IN_BRIEF);
        assert(GENDER_SLIP_IS_FLAG_ONLY);
    }

    test "a dry run is free: no paid tool on any seller turn" {
        assert(!DRY_RUN_SPENDS);
        assert(DRY_RUN_HIDES_PAID_TOOLS);
        assert(TURNS_MAX == 8);
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(0, true));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(1, true));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(2, true));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(3, true));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(4, true));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(5, true));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(6, true));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(7, true));
    }

    test "a real run keeps paid tools after discovery" {
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(0, false));
        assert(!paid_tool_offered(1, false));
        assert(paid_tool_offered(2, false));
        assert(paid_tool_offered(3, false));
        assert(paid_tool_offered(4, false));
        assert(paid_tool_offered(5, false));
        assert(paid_tool_offered(6, false));
        assert(paid_tool_offered(7, false));
    }

    test "a dry run's paid call is refused and nothing is charged" {
        assert(DRY_RUN_REFUSES_PAID_CALL);
        assert(DISCOVERY_REFUSES_PAID_CALL);
        assert(paid_call_refused(0, true, false));
        assert(paid_call_refused(2, true, false));
        assert(paid_call_refused(7, true, false));
        assert(paid_call_refused(1, false, false));
        assert(!paid_call_refused(2, false, false));
        assert(!paid_call_refused(7, false, false));
        assert(paid_call_refused(2, false, true));
    }

    test "any tool with a price > 0 is refused in a dry run" {
        assert(PAID_TOOL_IS_PRICED);
        assert(tool_is_paid(1));
        assert(tool_is_paid(1200));  // crm_voice_clone: the one-time clone price
        assert(!tool_is_paid(0));
        assert(tool_is_paid(borrowed_price(0, 16)));  // story_reel, split_reel: borrow lipsync_generate
        assert(!tool_is_paid(borrowed_price(0, 0)));
        assert(borrowed_price(12, 8) == 12);
        assert(!priced_tool_offered(1, 0, true));
        assert(!priced_tool_offered(16, 2, true));
        assert(!priced_tool_offered(1200, 7, true));
        assert(priced_tool_offered(0, 0, true));  // a free tool stays offered in a dry run
        assert(priced_tool_offered(0, 7, true));
        assert(!priced_tool_offered(16, 1, false));  // discovery hides it in a real run too
        assert(priced_tool_offered(16, 2, false));
    }

    test "VERSION says what the header's last note says" {
        assert(VERSION == 5);
    }

    test "a negated claim word is not a claim; pressure is never exempt" {
        assert(CLAIM_NEGATION_EXEMPT);
        assert(!PRESSURE_NEGATION_EXEMPT);
        assert(NEGATION_WINDOW_WORDS == 2);
        assert(claim_hit_counts(0));
        assert(!claim_hit_counts(1));
        assert(!claim_hit_counts(2));
        assert(claim_hit_counts(3));
        assert(HOOK_NE_SLUCHAJNO_FORBIDDEN_IN_BRIEF);
    }

    test "what was seen live is separated from what is not claimed" {
        assert(DRY_RUN_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(FULL_DRY_RUN_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(DISCOVERY_GATE_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(FAMILIARITY_REWRITE_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(SELLER_GENDER_FIXED_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(DRY_RUN_DELIVERY_CLAIM_SEEN);
        assert(!DRY_RUN_DELIVERY_CLAIM_FIXED);
        assert(RUN_KILLED_BY_REDEPLOY_SEEN);
        assert(FAILED_STATE_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(!CLAIM_CHECK_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(!RETRY_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(DUET_RAN_LIVE);
        assert(DUET_LIVE_RUN == "duet-mub68idg");
    }

    test "content is for the real game and nothing live is claimed" {
        assert(BUYER_GAME == "Leela Chakra");
        assert(LEELA_PLANES == 72);
        assert(LEELA_RULESET == "classic");
        assert(!DRY_RUN_SENDS);
    }

    test "honesty constants from the live run" {
        assert(FEED_PUBLISH_SAYS_SAVED);
        assert(NO_LIVED_EXPERIENCE_CLAIM);
        assert(PLAN_MEANING_FROM_CANON);
        assert(PERSONA_CONSENT_IS_NOT_CONSENT);
        assert(AGENT_PUBLISH_IS_HIDDEN);
    }
}

// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY
